   852                              <1> ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return AL = 0 if it
   853                              <1> ; was ')' and 2 if it was ']'. Brackets of both kinds count together;
   854                              <1> ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for '\' with
   855                              <1> ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
   856                              <1> ; anyway). ECX counts the open levels, from 1 for the one we are in.
   857                              <1> ;
   858                              <1> ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
   859                              <1> ; which is always the one just before where it starts: '(' must end at ')',
   860                              <1> ; '[' at ']', and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
   861                              <1> ; quote counts as running into it. '\' takes either closer. V_SKAT keeps the
   862                              <1> ; place where the skip started, for the report.
